From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 20:11:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: power: apple,t8140-pmp-report: Add
 apple,bw-vote

On T8132 the PMP takes a memory bandwidth vote in SOC-DEV-DVFS entries
409 and 411, which macOS raises while the video decoder or encoder runs.
Add apple,bw-vote to report entries: the main level of that vote the
entry's device needs while its domain is powered.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 .../bindings/power/apple,t8140-pmp-report.yaml         | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/apple,t8140-pmp-report.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/apple,t8140-pmp-report.yaml
index 3e1ac196ea..3aa73e0e1d 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/apple,t8140-pmp-report.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/apple,t8140-pmp-report.yaml
@@ -149,6 +149,16 @@ patternProperties:
           complete request word (with the valid bit) to the entry once; before
           clearing the device request it writes every level as 0.
 
+      apple,bw-vote:
+        $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32
+        minimum: 1
+        maximum: 31
+        description:
+          Main level of the memory bandwidth vote (T8132 SOC-DEV-DVFS entries
+          409 and 411) the device needs while the domain is powered. The host
+          writes the highest level of the powered entries with this property
+          and its own vote to both entries, and lowers it when they power off.
+
       apple,dvfs-request-levels:
         $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32-array
         minItems: 2
-- 
